course: dictionary
lesson: 2185
title: Cossack, a noun and an adjective
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Cossack is a noun when it names people: the Cossacks were free, self-ruling warriors and farmers on the steppes of what is now Ukraine and southern Russia, famous as horsemen. That is why it has a capital letter, like other names of peoples.
explain: Cossack is an adjective when it describes a thing: «a Cossack hat» and «a Cossack dance». Ask yourself: is this word naming a person, or telling me what kind of thing it is? A hat is not a Cossack, so here the word describes the hat.
explain: Context gives you clues. «Cossack images such as the hopak dance, the forelock and the bulava mace are central in Ukrainian culture» tells you Cossack is linked to Ukrainian culture and its dances. «Cossacks served as soldiers for different rulers» tells you they were fighters.
fact: Cossack is a noun (a Cossack, Cossacks) and an adjective (Cossack).
fact: The Cossacks were free, self-ruling warriors and farmers on the steppes of what is now Ukraine and southern Russia.
fact: «Hopak» is a lively Ukrainian folk dance with big jumps and squat-kicks, linked to Cossack traditions.
fact: The «Zaporizhian Cossacks» had a stronghold, the Sich, on the Dnipro river, and their council elected their leaders, called hetmans.
fact: «Bohdan Khmelnytsky» led a huge uprising in 1648, and the war brought terrible massacres too, so honest history tells both the hero's story and the dark pages.
exercise: «Cossack hat» and «Cossack dance» are phrases. What kind of word is Cossack in «a Cossack hat»? | *An adjective, describing the hat | A noun, naming a person | A verb, meaning to ride | A place name
exercise: What were the Cossacks? | A kind of hot drink | Dancers who only performed in towns | Kings who ruled Ukraine from a castle | *Free, self-ruling warriors and farmers on the steppes
exercise: Find and copy the word that names a lively Ukrainian dance: «Hopak is a lively Ukrainian folk dance with big jumps and squat-kicks, linked to Cossack traditions.» | jumps | *hopak | lively | squat
test: «Cossacks served as soldiers for different rulers, and their history includes both bravery and cruel deeds.» What does this tell you about Cossack history? | It only has happy stories | It had no fighting at all | *It has both good and bad parts | It was only about dancing
test: In «Cossack dance», what does the word Cossack describe? | A river | *The dance | A horse | A king
exam: The Zaporizhian Sich was a Cossack stronghold. Where was the Sich? | Under the sea | On the moon | *On the Dnipro river | In London
